WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.113
Tot el grup: Hello!

2
00:00:01.413 --> 00:00:03.271
We are Laia, Pau and Nora.

3
00:00:03.571 --> 00:00:09.184
Our celebration is St Lucia’s Day, and this is our idea for a Lucia Morning at our school.

4
00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:14.152
Laia: St Lucia’s Day is celebrated on the thirteenth of December.

5
00:00:14.452 --> 00:00:18.152
It takes place in Sweden, and also in Norway and Finland.

6
00:00:18.452 --> 00:00:22.150
In December, the days in Sweden are very short and dark.

7
00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:26.479
For the people who celebrate it, Lucia brings light and hope in the winter.

8
00:00:26.779 --> 00:00:33.274
We think it should have a place at our school because our days are short in December too, and it is a happy celebration.

9
00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:37.805
Pau: I’m Pau, and I’m going to talk about the customs.

10
00:00:38.105 --> 00:00:40.141
First, one person is Lucia.

11
00:00:40.441 --> 00:00:44.356
Lucia wears a long white dress and a crown with candles.

12
00:00:44.656 --> 00:00:46.995
Today the candles are often electric.

13
00:00:47.295 --> 00:00:53.070
Second, there is a procession: other children walk behind Lucia, and they sing songs.

14
00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:55.540
Third, people eat saffron buns.

15
00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:58.081
They are yellow and they have an S shape.

16
00:00:58.381 --> 00:01:09.478
Lucia has one thing in common with a celebration here: in Catalonia, Santa Llúcia is on the same day, and in Barcelona there is a big Christmas fair.

17
00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:12.588
Nora: I’m Nora, and this is our day.

18
00:01:12.888 --> 00:01:17.090
Our Lucia Morning is on Friday the eleventh of December, in the school hall.

19
00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:22.329
At nine o’clock, there is a procession with a song, with students from 4th ESO.

20
00:01:22.629 --> 00:01:26.671
At half past ten, Class 4A gives saffron buns to everyone.

21
00:01:26.971 --> 00:01:31.956
At half past eleven, 1st ESO students make paper stars with their teachers.

22
00:01:32.256 --> 00:01:35.404
A stereotype is that Lucia is always a blond girl.

23
00:01:35.704 --> 00:01:39.309
This is not fair, because people in Sweden are very different.

24
00:01:39.609 --> 00:01:43.149
In our plan, any student can be Lucia, a boy or a girl.

25
00:01:43.449 --> 00:01:44.193
Thank you!
